course: dictionary
lesson: 6113
title: Microbes: too small to see
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A microbe is a living thing so small that you need a microscope to see it. Bacteria, viruses and some fungi, such as yeast, are all microbes. «Microbes are living things far too small to see; a thousand bacteria in a row would just about stretch across a pinhead.»
explain: Microbes are not all bad. Some cause disease, but most are harmless or useful. «Most microbes are harmless or helpful: they make yoghurt and cheese, rot dead things, and trillions of them live in your gut helping to digest food.» So when you meet the word microbe, do not assume it means something dangerous.
explain: Another everyday word for a microbe is germ, and scientists also say micro-organism. When you wash your hands, you remove harmful microbes from your skin. Ask yourself: is this microbe causing harm, or is it doing a useful job?
fact: A microbe is a living thing too small to see without a microscope.
fact: Bacteria, viruses and some fungi, such as yeast, are all microbes.
fact: Some microbes cause diseases, but most are harmless or useful.
fact: Yeast makes bread rise, and bacteria help make yoghurt and cheese.
fact: Microbe is the same as micro-organism, and the everyday word for it is germ.
exercise: What is a microbe? | A metal used to make tools | *A living thing too small to see without a microscope | A huge animal that lives in the sea | A type of rock
exercise: «Most microbes are harmless or helpful.» What does this tell you? | All microbes make people ill | Microbes are easy to see with your eyes | Microbes can only be found in the sea | *Most microbes do not harm us
exercise: Which everyday word means the same as microbe? | Castle | Spoon | *Germ | Cloud
test: Which microbe helps bread rise? | Virus | *Yeast | Bacteria | Rock
test: Why do we wash our hands? | To make them shiny | *To remove harmful microbes | To warm them up | To make microbes grow faster
exam: Which statement about microbes is true? | *Most microbes are harmless or helpful | Microbes are never useful | Every microbe causes disease | Microbes are big enough to see easily
